  "lineage": "Mid-1990s indie rock subgenre characterized by complex polymetric rhythmic structures (irregular time signatures, frequent meter changes), angular and arpeggiated guitar-line architecture, and explicit prog-rock-influenced compositional ambition. Slint's Spiderland (1991) inaugurated the canonical sound; Don Caballero (Pittsburgh), Shellac (Steve Albini), Polvo, and the broader Touch and Go-Quarterstick label rosters defined the canonical American math rock roster. The Japanese math-rock scene (Toe, Tricot) extended international influence.",
